<%# Visual authority: Kurukoo public documentation composition — warm reference canvas, dense but readable code hierarchy, and explicit access/evidence boundaries. %>
<%- include('_partials/head', { pageStyles: ['/css/kurukoo-public-pages.css?v=5'] }) %>
<%- include('_partials/nav') %>
<main class="public-composition public-composition--api-docs container" aria-labelledby="api-docs-title">
  <section class="public-api-hero">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Developer platform</span><h1 id="api-docs-title">Build with Kurukoo, with the boundary visible.</h1><p>Use the public reference to understand the resource model, request shape and authentication boundary before integrating a supported Kurukoo capability into your own application.</p></div>
    <aside class="public-api-access-note"><span class="eyebrow">Integration readiness</span><strong>Access is separate from documentation.</strong><p>Endpoint availability, credentials and operational readiness are verified at execution time. Never place a secret in browser code or a public repository.</p><a class="public-return-link" href="/contact">Discuss an integration</a></aside>
  </section>
  <section class="public-api-layout" aria-label="API documentation reference">
    <aside class="public-api-sidebar" aria-label="API documentation sections"><p class="public-api-sidebar__label">Introduction</p><a href="#getting-started">Getting started</a><a href="#authentication">Authentication</a><a href="#rate-limits">Rate limits</a><p class="public-api-sidebar__label">Resources</p><a href="#profiles">Profiles</a><a href="#skills">Skills</a><a href="#messaging">Messaging</a><a href="#payments">Payments</a></aside>
    <div class="public-api-content">
      <section id="getting-started" class="public-api-section" aria-labelledby="api-getting-started"><span class="category-tag">Reference</span><h2 id="api-getting-started">Getting started</h2><p>The Kurukoo API exposes supported platform resources through resource-oriented URLs, form-encoded request bodies and JSON responses. Integrations should verify the current environment and access boundary before treating an endpoint as available.</p><pre class="public-api-code"><code>GET https://api.kurukoo.com/v1/health</code></pre></section>
      <section id="authentication" class="public-api-section" aria-labelledby="api-authentication"><span class="category-tag">Security boundary</span><h2 id="api-authentication">Authentication</h2><p>API keys authenticate approved requests. Manage keys through the relevant Kurukoo Dashboard boundary, limit their scope, and keep them out of client-side code, source control and any public surface.</p><pre class="public-api-code"><code>Authorization: Bearer KURUKOO_SECRET_KEY</code></pre></section>
      <section id="rate-limits" class="public-api-section" aria-labelledby="api-rate-limits"><span class="category-tag">Operational boundary</span><h2 id="api-rate-limits">Rate limits &amp; recovery</h2><p>Build integrations to handle response codes, retry only when the response semantics allow it, and show a clear recovery state rather than assuming delivery or completion. Current limits and availability belong to the executing environment.</p></section>
      <section id="profiles" class="public-api-section" aria-labelledby="api-profiles"><span class="category-tag">Resource</span><h2 id="api-profiles">Profiles</h2><p>Retrieve details about a specific memory profile only through an authorized integration path and only where the corresponding consent and access boundaries are satisfied.</p><pre class="public-api-code"><code>GET /v1/profiles/+2348012345678</code></pre><div class="public-api-schema" role="group" aria-label="Profile response schema"><div><code>phone</code><span>String · E.164 format</span></div><div><code>name</code><span>String</span></div><div><code>credits</code><span>Integer</span></div><div><code>tier</code><span>"base" | "plus" | "business"</span></div></div></section>
      <section id="skills" class="public-api-section public-api-section--compact" aria-labelledby="api-skills"><span class="category-tag">Resource</span><h2 id="api-skills">Skills</h2><p>Capabilities are governed by their canonical eligibility, policy and readiness state. An integration should surface unavailable or incomplete state rather than infer a matching outcome.</p></section>
      <section id="messaging" class="public-api-section public-api-section--compact" aria-labelledby="api-messaging"><span class="category-tag">Lifecycle</span><h2 id="api-messaging">Messaging</h2><p>Message preparation, channel delivery and receipt evidence are distinct stages. Treat a channel as active only when its configured adapter and observed delivery state permit it.</p></section>
      <section id="payments" class="public-api-section public-api-section--compact" aria-labelledby="api-payments"><span class="category-tag">Economic boundary</span><h2 id="api-payments">Payments</h2><p>Preparation, provider confirmation, settlement and recovery are separate economic states. Client experiences must not label an action paid or settled until the canonical evidence is available.</p></section>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="public-api-footer-cta" aria-labelledby="api-support-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">Need integration guidance?</span><h2 id="api-support-title">Start with the request and the boundary you need to preserve.</h2><p>Use Web Chat for a conversational starting point, or contact the partnership team with the supported capability and environment you are considering.</p></div><div class="public-api-footer-cta__actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/chat">Open Web Chat</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/contact">Contact partnerships</a></div></section>
</main>
<%- include('_partials/footer') %>
